# Vercel upload ignore rules (repo root).
#
# The Vercel project's Root Directory is "web", so Vercel serves whatever is
# inside web/ — this file only keeps the *upload* small and prevents
# unrelated folders from being shipped.
#
# NOTE: the CLI deploys from the repo root (not from web/) precisely because
# Root Directory=web means Vercel expects to find a web/ folder in the
# uploaded tree. Deploying from inside web/ fails with
# "The specified Root Directory \"web\" does not exist".

# Build/tooling folders that are not part of the deployed site
# (root-anchored "/..." so they cannot match web/scripts, web/js, etc.)
/next-web/
/native/
/tests/
/builds/
/dist/
/supabase/

# Keep web/scripts (build tooling + env handling) out of the public site too.
# web/.vercelignore already does this for the web/ root; repeat it here so the
# rule holds regardless of which .vercelignore Vercel applies.
/web/scripts/
/web/README.md
/web/.env*

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Secrets and local state
.env.payments
.env*
!.env.example
.vercel/

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
